  "title": "The world's most valuable hosting startups, ranked by AI | Uback",
  "description": "Uback ranks the world's non-listed hosting and developer-cloud companies by AI-estimated valuation: Vercel, Vultr, Render, Netlify, Railway and more. Edition 0 (beta).",
  "h1": "The world’s most valuable hosting startups",
  "intro": "Developer clouds and application platforms (PaaS), and cloud and web hosting providers. Ranked worldwide by AI-estimated valuation. The market sets the value; our AI estimates it.",
  "not_in_segment": "GPU and AI clouds (CoreWeave, Lambda, Crusoe, Nebius) belong to Compute & inference; CDN and edge networks (Cloudflare, Fastly, Gcore) to Edge & CDN; databases (Supabase, Neon) to Data. Hosts that never raised a funding round from outside investors are not ranked: Hostinger, Hetzner, SiteGround, Kinsta, Leaseweb, and Contabo (KKR) and Liquid Web (Madison Dearborn), bought by private equity without a funding round. Not eligible because created or entirely owned by a group: Newfold Digital (Bluehost, HostGator), Scaleway (Iliad), Heroku (Salesforce), Exoscale (A1). Under review: WP Engine, controlled by Silver Lake since 2018; Uback has not confirmed that outside minority shareholders remain. Acquired companies are no longer ranked: Koyeb (Mistral AI, 2026), Latitude.sh (Megaport, 2025), Fermyon (Akamai, 2025), Cloudways (DigitalOcean), Linode (Akamai). A company appears in one segment only.",
  "activity": "developer clouds, application platforms and cloud hosting",
  "og_title": "The world’s most valuable<br>hosting startups",
  "sources": "Bloomberg, BusinessWire, SiliconANGLE, TechCrunch, DataCenterDynamics, FinSMEs, Tech.eu, EU-Startups, Contrary Research, company announcements."
 },
